<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jahangir Mahal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a> Mahal is a palace in Orchha, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, built in the early 17th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vir-singh-deo">Bir Singh Deo of Orchha</a>. It is said to have been raised in honour of the Mughal emperor Jahangir, his patron and ally. Its tiered courtyard plan, domed pavilions and carved stone screens combine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> and Mughal styles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jahangir-mahal.jpg" alt="Jahangir Mahal" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pierre Dalbéra from Paris, France · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Jehangir_Mahal_(Orchha)_(8451914174).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
